<title>JAPAN: Bond fund applies for Osaka listing for first time.</title>
<headline>Bond fund applies for Osaka listing for first time.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fund aiming to invest in fixed income securities in Asian countries has applied for listing on the Osaka Securities Exchange (OSE), OSE said on Monday.</p>
<p>The fund, named &quot;Asia High Yield Bond Fund&quot;, would be the first investment fund investing in bonds to be listed on the OSE, it said. It aims to invest in short- to long-term bonds in Asian countries, the exchange said.</p>
<p>The fund plans to be listed on October 3, and to issue 25 million shares upon listing. It also plans to be listed on the Luxembourg and Singapore bourses on the same day.</p>
</text>
